<title>UK: National Bank of Greece sets $200 mln 10-year FRN.</title>
<headline>National Bank of Greece sets $200 mln 10-year FRN.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following structured subordinated floating-rate issue was announced by lead manager Chase and Salomon Brothers International.</p>
<p> BORROWER   NATIONAL BANK OF GREECE</p>
<p> AMT	  $200 MLN  BASE	 =M-LIBOR  MATURITY	*JUN.07</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 MARGIN    *+60 BP    PAY DATE    24.JUN.97</p>
<p> MOODY	=	   ISS PRICE  99.576    FULL FEES   0.40</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  =	   REOFFER    99.576</p>
<p> NOTES     *MARGIN RISES TO 190 BP IF NOT CALLED AT PAR IN 2002.</p>
<p> LISTING    LUX	 DENOMS (K) 10	  SALE LIMITS US/GB/GR</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  GREECE    TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.30	SELL CONC  0.10	PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
